---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout
  title="Sync Across Devices — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How cntxt keeps your Projects, Quests, and session history following you across devices."
  path="/learn/sync"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Sync across devices</h1>
  <p>
    Sign in and your Projects, Quests, and Resources follow you to another
    machine — not just surviving a browser restart, but showing up on a
    laptop you haven't used in weeks. Conflicting edits from two devices
    resolve last-write-wins. Your <a href="/learn/sessions">session history</a>
    syncs too, as a simpler, append-only copy — a session is immutable once
    captured, so there's nothing to merge.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is the one part of cntxt that runs on our servers continuously, for
    as long as you keep syncing — which is why it's the feature a
    subscription pays for, not a one-time purchase. Everything else on this
    page works the same whether you've ever signed in or not.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Account / sign-in</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cross-device sync of Projects, Quests, and Resources</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cross-device sync of session history</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Sync that keeps working fully in the background, dashboard closed</td>
        <td>🟡 In progress</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Shared/team workspaces</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
